{"ok":true,"data":{"commands":[{"name":"publish","words":[],"flags":[{"name":"--md","value":"<file>","need":"required","summary":"the note to publish"},{"name":"--folder-id","value":"<folder id>","need":"required","summary":"the Drive folder the document is created in"},{"name":"--house","value":"<file>","need":"optional","summary":"a house style file other than the one inside gdoc"}],"summary":"Build the note as a house-style document and upload it into one folder.","notes":["A line the note writes as - [ ] words is a task, and the document gets a box a reader ticks. At the end of that line, after the words, one owner and one due date become chips: @anna@example.com or a bare @anna with --domain or the domain setting in effect, and 2026-11-20, in either order. A - [x] line is done and its words are struck through. A bare owner with no domain in effect, two owners, two dates, a date that is not a calendar day, a nested task and a task in a numbered list are each refused by name before anything is uploaded.","A chip is text that knows an address: this publish emails nobody, shares the document with nobody and assigns nothing. checks.tasks on the envelope is the read-back of the boxes and the chips, and it is true for a note with no task."],"example":"gdoc publish --md note.md --folder-id 1AbC..."}],"settings":{"mark":"⁘","mark_from":"default"},"update":{"installed":"v2.9.0","latest_stable":"v2.10.0","latest_nightly":"v2.10.1","checked_at":"2026-10-03T00:00:00Z"}},"version":"v2.9.0"}
